Generated artifacts

WebAssembly modules emitted by the AOT compiler can contain function bodies and
read-only data copied from the four checked-in runtime modules under
crates/pinewasm_aot/runtime: pinewasm_aot_runtime.wasm,
pinewasm_aot_runtime_standalone_wasm.wasm, pinewasm_aot_runtime_ta.wasm, and
pinewasm_aot_runtime_broker.wasm. Those modules compile the first-party
pinewasm_aot_runtime, pinewasm_num, pinewasm_ta, and pinewasm_broker crates
(AGPL-3.0-only) together with the runtime's third-party closure: libm (MIT),
ryu (Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0), and itoa (MIT OR Apache-2.0). The bytes that
merely represent a caller's own script carry no AI Edge LLC claim. The
command `cargo xtask artifact-notice --out DIR` writes the notice bundle
(LICENSE, NOTICE, the runtime-closure license texts, and
artifact-manifest.json) that accompanies conveyed artifacts.

The authoritative block above records the notice model.
docs/artifact-distribution.md draws the byte boundary.

